### Reproduction

Setup:
- Next.js `16.1.6`, React `19.2.4`, better-auth `1.5.4`
- Postgres for `database`, Redis for `secondaryStorage`
- `nextCookies()` last in plugins list
- App sits behind an nginx sidecar with the default `proxy_read_timeout = 60s`

Steps:
1. Sign in. `__Secure-better-auth.session_token` and `__Secure-better-auth.session_data` cookies are set.
2. Use the app within the cookie cache window (5 min) — every authenticated page renders fine.
3. Wait until the cookie cache expires (>5 min idle).
4. Open any page whose Server Component calls `auth.api.getSession({ headers: await headers() })` (a `layout.tsx` or `page.tsx`).

Reproduction with `curl`, same cookie, three endpoints:

```bash
# 1) Route handler — fine, ~150ms, returns full session JSON
curl -H "Cookie: __Secure-better-auth.session_token=$TOKEN" \
     https://app/api/auth/get-session

# 2) Server component path — hangs exactly 60s, returns truncated HTML
curl -o body.html -w "%{http_code} %{time_total}\n" \
     -H "Cookie: __Secure-better-auth.session_token=$TOKEN" \
     https://app/dashboard
# -> 200 60.20s, 18324 bytes, no </body>, no </html>

# 3) Same path with an invalid cookie — fast, behaves as logged-out
curl -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} %{time_total}\n" \
     -H "Cookie: __Secure-better-auth.session_token=invalid" \
     https://app/dashboard
# -> 200 0.20s
```

The hang is reproducible with `curl` alone, so it's not browser-specific.

### Current vs. Expected behavior

The server starts streaming the response (HTTP 200, headers and the first chunk of HTML are sent), then stops emitting bytes. After 60 seconds the upstream proxy closes the connection mid-stream. The browser receives partial HTML (no closing `</body>`/`</html>`) and renders a blank or skeleton page.

Inspecting the truncated body, the stream consistently stops at the same point on every authenticated route — a reference to the `MetadataBoundary` / `IconMark` component (`I[792510, ..., "IconMark"]`) sitting at position `3` of the metadata array:

```
...
<script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4:[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{}]\n
11:[[...meta entries...]]\n
13:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{...}],
   [\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{...}],
   [\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{...}],
   [\"$\",\"$L18\",\"3\",{}]]\n"])</script>
<-- stream ends here, nginx closes after 60s -->
```

The metadata Suspense boundary never resolves, which keeps the stream open until the proxy gives up.

Pattern: the issue only triggers when `getSession` would actually need to write something back to the client — cookie cache refresh after `cookieCache.maxAge` expiry, or rolling session refresh once `now > session.updatedAt + updateAge`. With a fresh login (cache valid) or a missing/invalid cookie (no write attempted) the same routes return in ~200ms.

The route-handler path (`/api/auth/get-session`) does the same lookup, refreshes the same cookies, and returns in ~150ms. The Server Component call path is the only one that hangs.

Expected: either `auth.api.getSession` should not attempt cookie writes from a context where Next.js refuses them (Server Components can read cookies but can't set them), or the failure should be raised immediately so the rendering pipeline can finish.

