### To Reproduce

1. Configure better-auth with oidcProvider plugin
2. Complete OAuth2 authorization flow and obtain an access token
3. Call GET /oauth2/userinfo with header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
4. Observe: Request fails because sessionMiddleware requires cookie-based auth
5. Expected: Request should succeed per OIDC spec (Bearer token auth)

The regression was introduced in commit 4817a6e9a4 (PR #2107 "fix(openapi): add operationId to routes") on Nov 15, 2025. 

[The diff](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/pull/2107/files/52fd3d3f9c083067a3ddc8338db3160302a1c433#diff-49cfca7fb0480f3cfc9ac8610d8f3f911091e60ef89845304909e19c4458525dR909-R910) shows `sessionMiddleware` was (likely unintentionally) added alongside `operationId`:
```diff
method: "GET",
+  operationId: "oauth2Userinfo",
+  use: [sessionMiddleware],         // <-- Problem: requires valid session via cookies or throws 401
metadata: { ...
```

### Current vs. Expected behavior

**Current**
The /oauth2/userinfo endpoint requires cookie-based session authentication via sessionMiddleware, causing OAuth2/OIDC clients using Bearer tokens to fail.

**Expected**
Per [OpenID Connect Core spec](https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#UserInfo), the userinfo endpoint MUST accept `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` header authentication.

**Fix**
Remove `use: [sessionMiddleware]` from line 934 in packages/better-auth/src/plugins/oidc-provider/index.ts

